meta {
  name: A2 - Create Initiative
  type: graphql
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}
  body: graphql
  auth: inherit
}

body:graphql {
  mutation SeedInitiative {
    initiativeCreate(input: {
      name: "estuary-connector-verification"
      description: "Temporary record created to verify source-linear's Initiatives stream. Safe to delete."
    }) {
      success
      initiative { id name createdAt updatedAt archivedAt status }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Reference: https://linear.app/developers/graphql

  **Only the user runs this. Never the assistant.** This is a state-mutating call.

  Creates one throwaway initiative so the Initiatives stream can be observed with real
  data. Same rationale as `A1 - Create Project`.

  Closes: the Initiatives stream has NO observed response body
  (`30 - Initiatives Bare` and `31 - Initiatives Incremental Sweep` both return zero rows).

  **This request doubles as an ENTITLEMENT check, which is the more valuable outcome.**
  Initiatives are a paid-plan feature, so "zero initiatives" is currently ambiguous — it
  may mean the workspace has none, or that the plan does not include them. If this mutation
  fails with a feature/permission error rather than succeeding, that resolves the ambiguity
  and the Initiatives stream needs a different treatment (graceful degradation when the
  workspace lacks entitlement, rather than assuming an empty-but-available collection).
  Please report the error verbatim if it fails.

  **Re-run after:** `30 - Initiatives Bare`, then `31 - Initiatives Incremental Sweep`.

  Cleanup: archive or delete the initiative from the Linear UI once verification is done.
}
